litellm_proxy/
firecrawl-stack/

Public/

tirith/
repo-backup-*/
hermes-env-backup/
archive/
# archive/ is ignored wholesale, which is what we want. The one exception is
# the README that explains WHY, so the rule is self-documenting in the repo
# rather than only in a scratch file. `archive/*` cannot be used for this: it
# would also match the subdirectory and stop git descending, so the negation
# below could never match. `archive/**` ignores contents while leaving the
# directory itself visible, which is the form that works.
!archive/
archive/**
!archive/README.md
# Anchored to the repo root. An unanchored `research/` matches at ANY depth,
# so it silently swallowed profiles/research/SOUL.md: the profile existed,
# was published by the sync script, and was never tracked. Nothing failed
# and nothing warned -- git simply never saw the file, exactly like the
# bundled-category skills that publish_profiles_and_skills.py could not
# reach. A pattern's DEPTH is part of its meaning, and this one had none.
/research/
/research_output/

