# ── Corpus distillation runtime state (cognition-arena) ────────────────────
# Templates and the install guide ARE tracked. The filled-in state is not:
# it holds one row per corpus file, the results of the read, and archives of
# prior passes — all specific to one machine's corpus.
# TRACKED as of 2026-09-26 (the operator's call, overriding 7a187e6): the arena is the
# accumulated output of hundreds of 15-minute runs and had ZERO commit history.
# One bad rewrite and there was no way back. It is now versioned like any other
# deliverable. Priors/archives stay ignored — they are superseded snapshots.
cognition-arena/.prior-run-latest
cognition-arena/prior-run-*/
cognition-arena/CP-*.md
DB-MIGRATION-HANDOFF.md
IMPLEMENT-HANDOFF.md
RETRIEVAL-SETUP-HANDOFF.md
RESEARCH-provenance-of-inference.md
research-resultideas.md

# Timestamped safety snapshots written by the T2 repair scripts. These
# are working backups taken immediately before a write, not audit
# evidence: the audit trail belongs in git history and in the
# committed docs/audit/*.json reports. One landed here from a test
# fixture, which is how the pattern was noticed.
docs/audit/*.bak.json

# ── Owner working documents (tracked nowhere; referenced by path) ──
# SCRATCHPAD.md is the operator's live scratchpad: append/revise as research lands.
# It is referenced by absolute path from the wiki-cognition skill, the
# research-lane cron prompts, and docs/, so it MUST stay at the repo root --
# it is untracked, not relocated. Backup copies follow it.
SCRATCHPAD.md
SCRATCHPAD.md.bak.*

# Generated lint work-queue: a snapshot of okf_lint.py --check output, appended
# by scripts/okf_repair.py and regenerable by re-running the linter. It is a
# run artifact, not a schema -- schemas/ holds okf-schema.yaml and friends.
schemas/okf-queue.jsonl
